Interactive USD edits of points and curves, with the usd procedural cache_id and with the render delegate

Points have their positions, widths and displayColor edited, and a linear curve its points, widths and topology,
the stage being re-rendered after each edit.
The scenario runs with the "usd" procedural reading the stage through its cache_id in an interactive render session,
and with the HdArnoldRendererPlugin render delegate driven like a Hydra host, see
testsuite/common/interactive_usd_test.h. Each render is checked in test.cpp, and the last procedural render is
compared against the reference image. Edits that aren't rendered correctly yet are reported as warnings (known issues
in test.cpp).

author: sebastien.blaineau.ortega@autodesk.com

PARAMS: {'program_env': 'interactive_usd'}
